IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `theft-nouns`
IMPORT `theft-seat`

-- Theft Act 1968 -- tests of the seat layer (theft-seat.l4).
--
-- Each case states the facts a person in the seat would state, calls the exported
-- question with those plain inputs, and asserts the answer worked out by hand from
-- the text of the Act. Inputs not named in a case are "no" (FALSE); a date not
-- named is 1 January 2000, a number not named is 0 and a choice not named is the
-- first one listed. Those defaults are filler, and no test here checks that an
-- answer is independent of them.
-- A comment above each case says what it stands for.
--
-- The penalty fixtures below are written from the section texts, not read from
-- the encoding.

§ `Penalty fixtures`

GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`pen 7 years` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 7)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`pen life` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS `imprisonment for life`
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`pen 14 years` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 14)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`pen 10 years` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 10)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`pen 5 years` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 5)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`pen 2 years` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 2)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`pen 3 years` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 3)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`pen summary 6 months or level 5 or both` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of months` 6)
    `the fine ceiling` IS (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5)
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS TRUE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`pen summary level 3 only` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS `the section states no imprisonment`
    `the fine ceiling` IS (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3)
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`pen summary level 5 only` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS `the section states no imprisonment`
    `the fine ceiling` IS (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5)
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE

§ `Sections 1 to 6`


§§ `Section 1 -- theft`

-- A shopper takes a watch from a shop counter, meaning to keep it.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of theft` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other personal property` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Same, but the shopper believed they had the right in law to take it (s 2(1)(a)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of theft` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other personal property` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Same, but no intention to deprive permanently (s 6).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of theft` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other personal property` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Same, but the property belonged to no one else (s 5).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of theft` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other personal property` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Same, but the thing is land with none of the s 4(2) exceptions (s 4(2)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of theft` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `land itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Section 2 -- dishonestly`

-- Dishonest and none of the three beliefs.
#ASSERT `Was what I did dishonest` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Not dishonest otherwise, and no belief: nothing makes it dishonest.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was what I did dishonest` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Belief in a legal right to deprive the other (s 2(1)(a)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Was what I did dishonest` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Belief that the other would have consented (s 2(1)(b)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Was what I did dishonest` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Belief that the owner cannot be found by reasonable steps (s 2(1)(c)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Was what I did dishonest` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- That third belief does not help a trustee or personal representative (s 2(1)(c)).
#ASSERT `Was what I did dishonest` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§§ `Section 3 -- appropriates`

-- Assumed the rights of an owner (s 3(1)).
#ASSERT `Did I appropriate the property` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Assumed no right of an owner at all.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I appropriate the property` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Came by it innocently, later started keeping it as owner (s 3(1)).
#ASSERT `Did I appropriate the property` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Good-faith buyer for value; only the seller's title was defective (s 3(2)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I appropriate the property` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- The same buyer, but the defect is not the only ground: s 3(2) does not save the buyer.
#ASSERT `Did I appropriate the property` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

§§ `Section 4 -- property`

-- Money.
#ASSERT `Is the thing property that can be stolen` `money` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A thing in action.
#ASSERT `Is the thing property that can be stolen` `a thing in action or other intangible property` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Land, with no exception (s 4(2)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the thing property that can be stolen` `land itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A trustee sells land in breach of confidence (s 4(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `Is the thing property that can be stolen` `land itself` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Someone not in possession of the land severs something forming part of it (s 4(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Is the thing property that can be stolen` `a thing forming part of land` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The same, but the person is in possession of the land.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the thing property that can be stolen` `a thing forming part of land` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A tenant in possession appropriates a fixture let with the land (s 4(2)(c)).
#ASSERT `Is the thing property that can be stolen` `a thing forming part of land` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A wild creature not reduced into possession (s 4(4)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the thing property that can be stolen` `a wild creature that is neither tamed nor ordinarily kept in captivity, or the carcase of one` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The same, reduced into possession by another (s 4(4)).
#ASSERT `Is the thing property that can be stolen` `a wild creature that is neither tamed nor ordinarily kept in captivity, or the carcase of one` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- A tame wild creature (s 4(4)).
#ASSERT `Is the thing property that can be stolen` `a wild creature that is tamed or ordinarily kept in captivity` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Something that is not property.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the thing property that can be stolen` `something that is not property within section 4(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Section 5 -- belonging to another`

-- Another has possession or control (s 5(1)).
#ASSERT `Does the property belong to another` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- No one but the person has any interest.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the property belong to another` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Held on trust, and another can enforce it (s 5(2)).
#ASSERT `Does the property belong to another` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Received on account of another and bound to deal with it in a particular way (s 5(3)).
#ASSERT `Does the property belong to another` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Got by another's mistake and bound to make restoration (s 5(4)).
#ASSERT `Does the property belong to another` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Only an equitable interest under an agreement to transfer (s 5(1)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the property belong to another` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Section 6 -- intention of permanently depriving`

-- Meant the other to lose it for good.
#ASSERT `Did I intend permanently to deprive the other of it` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- No such intention.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I intend permanently to deprive the other of it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Meant to treat it as one's own to dispose of regardless of the other's rights (s 6(1)).
#ASSERT `Did I intend permanently to deprive the other of it` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A borrowing alone.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did I intend permanently to deprive the other of it` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A borrowing so long that it equals an outright taking (s 6(1)).
#ASSERT `Did I intend permanently to deprive the other of it` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Parted with it on a return condition one might not meet, for own purposes, without authority (s 6(2)).
#ASSERT `Did I intend permanently to deprive the other of it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Intended to defeat a trust that another could enforce (s 5(2)).
#ASSERT `Did I intend permanently to deprive the other of it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Meant not to make restoration after a mistake (s 5(4)).
#ASSERT `Did I intend permanently to deprive the other of it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- 41 assertions written; check.sh must report 41 satisfied, 0 failed, 0 refused.
§ `Sections 7 to 14`


§§ `Section 7 -- theft`

-- Theft: seven years on indictment.
#ASSERT (`What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of theft` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other personal property` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `pen 7 years`
-- Not theft.
#ASSERT (`What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of theft` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other personal property` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no offence under this section on these facts`

