§§ `Section 11 -- removal of articles from places open to the public`

-- Article from a permanent collection removed from a building the public may view.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- An article not part of a permanent collection, not removed on a public day (s 11(2)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The same, removed on a day the public have access.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- With lawful authority.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Believed in lawful authority (s 11(3)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Believed authority would be given if the person entitled knew (s 11(3)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- The public have no access to the building.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Public access to view a collection housed in the building.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A collection made for sales or commercial dealings is not a collection for s 11.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of removing an article from a place open to the public` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Five years on indictment.
#ASSERT (`What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of removing an article from a place open to the public` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `pen 5 years`
-- Not an offence.
#ASSERT (`What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of removing an article from a place open to the public` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no offence under this section on these facts`

§§ `Section 12 -- taking a conveyance without authority`

-- Takes a conveyance without the owner's consent.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The owner consented.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Other lawful authority.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Hired out, and the hirer (the owner for this section) consented (s 12(7)(b)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Hired out: the owner's consent alone does not suffice, because the hirer is the owner here.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Drove one knowing it had been taken without authority.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Allowed to be carried in one knowing it had been taken.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Drove one, not knowing it had been taken.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Believed in authority (s 12(6)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Believed the owner would have consented (s 12(6)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A pedal cycle: s 12(1) does not apply to it (s 12(5)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A conveyance built for use only under the control of a person not carried in it (a model).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Summary conviction: six months, or a level 5 fine, or both.
#ASSERT (`What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `pen summary 6 months or level 5 or both`
-- Not an offence.
#ASSERT (`What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of taking a conveyance without authority` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no offence under this section on these facts`

§§ `Section 12(4) -- on a trial for theft`

-- Tried for theft, jury not satisfied of theft, section 12(1) offence proved.
#ASSERT `May the jury find me guilty of taking a conveyance without authority on a charge of theft` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Not tried on indictment for theft.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the jury find me guilty of taking a conveyance without authority on a charge of theft` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- The jury are satisfied of theft: the alternative verdict is not needed.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the jury find me guilty of taking a conveyance without authority on a charge of theft` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Section 12(1) offence not proved.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the jury find me guilty of taking a conveyance without authority on a charge of theft` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Liable as on summary conviction for the s 12(1) offence.
#ASSERT (`What follows if the jury find me guilty of taking a conveyance without authority on a charge of theft` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `pen summary 6 months or level 5 or both`
-- Not an alternative verdict.
