§ `Sections 26 to 36`


§§ `Section 26 -- search for stolen goods`

-- Information on oath, reasonable cause, addressed to a constable.
#ASSERT `Can a justice grant a warrant to search my premises for stolen goods` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Addressed to someone else under an enactment that expressly so provides.
#ASSERT `Can a justice grant a warrant to search my premises for stolen goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Addressed to someone else with no enactment.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a justice grant a warrant to search my premises for stolen goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- No information on oath.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a justice grant a warrant to search my premises for stolen goods` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Reasonable cause not made to appear.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a justice grant a warrant to search my premises for stolen goods` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Authorised under section 26 to search.
#ASSERT `May the person with a warrant enter and search my premises` TRUE
-- Not authorised.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the person with a warrant enter and search my premises` FALSE)
-- Authorised and believes the goods stolen.
#ASSERT `May the person searching seize goods he believes to be stolen` TRUE TRUE
-- Authorised, but does not believe the goods stolen.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the person searching seize goods he believes to be stolen` TRUE FALSE)
-- Believes they are stolen, but not authorised.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the person searching seize goods he believes to be stolen` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Section 27 -- evidence and procedure`

-- Charged together with others, same theft.
#ASSERT `May I be charged and tried together with others for handling goods from the same theft` TRUE TRUE
-- Charged alone.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I be charged and tried together with others for handling goods from the same theft` TRUE FALSE)
-- Others are charged and I am not.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I be charged and tried together with others for handling goods from the same theft` FALSE TRUE)
-- Jointly indicted; the jury are satisfied I handled the goods.
#ASSERT `May the jury find me guilty although I did not handle the goods jointly` TRUE TRUE
-- The jury are not satisfied.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the jury find me guilty although I did not handle the goods jointly` TRUE FALSE)
-- Not jointly indicted.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the jury find me guilty although I did not handle the goods jointly` FALSE TRUE)
-- Another theft exactly twelve months before the offence charged (s 27(3)(a)).
#ASSERT `May evidence of my other dealings or earlier convictions be used to show I knew or believed the goods were stolen` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2019) (Date 15 3 2020) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) 0
-- Another theft a day more than twelve months before.
#ASSERT NOT (`May evidence of my other dealings or earlier convictions be used to show I knew or believed the goods were stolen` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 14 3 2019) (Date 15 3 2020) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) 0)
-- A conviction exactly five years before, seven days' notice (s 27(3)(b)).
#ASSERT `May evidence of my other dealings or earlier convictions be used to show I knew or believed the goods were stolen` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 3 2020) TRUE (Date 15 3 2015) 7
-- A conviction a day more than five years before.
#ASSERT NOT (`May evidence of my other dealings or earlier convictions be used to show I knew or believed the goods were stolen` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 3 2020) TRUE (Date 14 3 2015) 7)
-- Six days' notice is too few.
#ASSERT NOT (`May evidence of my other dealings or earlier convictions be used to show I knew or believed the goods were stolen` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 3 2020) TRUE (Date 15 3 2018) 6)
-- A conviction on the day of the offence charged is not one preceding it.
#ASSERT NOT (`May evidence of my other dealings or earlier convictions be used to show I knew or believed the goods were stolen` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 3 2020) TRUE (Date 15 3 2020) 7)
-- No evidence yet given of my having or dealing in the goods.
#ASSERT NOT (`May evidence of my other dealings or earlier convictions be used to show I knew or believed the goods were stolen` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 20 1 2020) (Date 15 3 2020) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) 0)
-- Proceeded against for more than handling.
#ASSERT NOT (`May evidence of my other dealings or earlier convictions be used to show I knew or believed the goods were stolen` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 20 1 2020) (Date 15 3 2020) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) 0)
-- Copy given seven days before the hearing.
#ASSERT `Can a statutory declaration be used against me as evidence of the facts it states` TRUE TRUE TRUE 7 FALSE 0 FALSE
-- Copy given only six days before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a statutory declaration be used against me as evidence of the facts it states` TRUE TRUE TRUE 6 FALSE 0 FALSE)
-- I required the declarant to attend, by notice three days before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a statutory declaration be used against me as evidence of the facts it states` TRUE TRUE TRUE 10 TRUE 3 FALSE)
-- My notice came only two days before: too late (s 27(4)(b)).
#ASSERT `Can a statutory declaration be used against me as evidence of the facts it states` TRUE TRUE TRUE 10 TRUE 2 FALSE
-- The same, but within further time the court allowed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a statutory declaration be used against me as evidence of the facts it states` TRUE TRUE TRUE 10 TRUE 2 TRUE)
-- Not proceedings for theft in transmission.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can a statutory declaration be used against me as evidence of the facts it states` FALSE TRUE TRUE 10 FALSE 0 FALSE)

§§ `Section 29 -- summary trial`

-- An ordinary indictable offence under the Act.
#ASSERT `Does paragraph 11 list my offence as one that may be tried summarily with my consent` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Robbery and the other three are excepted.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does paragraph 11 list my offence as one that may be tried summarily with my consent` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A dwelling burglary by force or deception or tool.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does paragraph 11 list my offence as one that may be tried summarily with my consent` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A dwelling burglary with violence or the threat of it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does paragraph 11 list my offence as one that may be tried summarily with my consent` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- A dwelling burglary with neither force nor violence.
#ASSERT `Does paragraph 11 list my offence as one that may be tried summarily with my consent` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Handling goods stolen abroad.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does paragraph 11 list my offence as one that may be tried summarily with my consent` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Not an indictable offence under the Act.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does paragraph 11 list my offence as one that may be tried summarily with my consent` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Section 30 -- spouses and civil partners`

-- Proceedings for stealing the spouse's property, no consent of the Director.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property` `proceedings are instituted against him` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- With the Director's consent.
#ASSERT `May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property` `proceedings are instituted against him` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Charged jointly with the spouse (s 30(4) proviso (a)(i)).
#ASSERT `May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property` `proceedings are instituted against him` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Under no obligation to cohabit by a decree (proviso (a)(ii)).
#ASSERT `May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property` `proceedings are instituted against him` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- A separation order with a civil partner (proviso (a)(iii)).
#ASSERT `May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property` `proceedings are instituted against him` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- An arrest without warrant by the spouse, no consent (s 30(5)).
#ASSERT NOT (`May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property` `an arrest without warrant made by his wife, husband or civil partner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The same with the Director's consent.
#ASSERT `May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property` `an arrest without warrant made by his wife, husband or civil partner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Some other step: the text does not bring it within s 30(4).
#ASSERT `May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property` `some other step` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Not an offence of stealing or damaging a spouse's property.
#ASSERT `May the step be taken against me over my spouse's or civil partner's property` `proceedings are instituted against him` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- My wife brings proceedings with the Director's consent.
#ASSERT `May my wife or husband bring proceedings against me as if we were not married` `proceedings are instituted against him` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- My wife brings proceedings for stealing from her, with no consent: subject to s 30(4).
#ASSERT NOT (`May my wife or husband bring proceedings against me as if we were not married` `proceedings are instituted against him` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Someone other than my wife or husband.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my wife or husband bring proceedings against me as if we were not married` `proceedings are instituted against him` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- My wife brings proceedings for some other offence.
#ASSERT `May my wife or husband bring proceedings against me as if we were not married` `proceedings are instituted against him` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The spouse who brings the proceedings is competent to give evidence for the prosecution.
#ASSERT `Is my wife or husband a competent witness for the prosecution` TRUE
-- Not the spouse bringing the proceedings.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my wife or husband a competent witness for the prosecution` FALSE)

§§ `Section 31 -- civil proceedings and rights`

-- In proceedings about property, excused only by the incrimination.
#ASSERT `Am I excused from answering because it may incriminate me or my spouse` TRUE TRUE
-- Other proceedings.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excused from answering because it may incriminate me or my spouse` FALSE TRUE)
-- Excused for some other reason.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excused from answering because it may incriminate me or my spouse` TRUE FALSE)
-- Offered against me for an offence under the Act: not admissible.
#ASSERT `Can what I said in civil proceedings be used against me for an offence under this Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Offered in proceedings for another offence.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can what I said in civil proceedings be used against me for an offence under this Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- A statement made elsewhere.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can what I said in civil proceedings be used against me for an offence under this Act` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Offered against my spouse: not admissible.
#ASSERT `Can what I said in civil proceedings be used against my spouse for an offence under this Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- We married after the statement was made: the bar does not protect that spouse.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can what I said in civil proceedings be used against my spouse for an offence under this Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Title unaffected by the conviction alone (s 31(2)).
#ASSERT `Does my conviction alone affect the title to the property` TRUE TRUE
-- Something else is said to affect the title.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my conviction alone affect the title to the property` TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Section 32 -- abolished offences`

-- Larceny, last day before the commencement: not abolished as to that offence.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the old offence abolished as regards what I did` `larceny` (Date 31 12 1968) FALSE)
-- Larceny, last day the day of commencement.
#ASSERT `Is the old offence abolished as regards what I did` `larceny` (Date 1 1 1969) FALSE
-- Robbery at common law.
#ASSERT `Is the old offence abolished as regards what I did` `robbery at common law` (Date 1 1 1969) FALSE
-- Receiving stolen property.
#ASSERT `Is the old offence abolished as regards what I did` `receiving stolen property` (Date 1 1 1969) FALSE
-- Cheating, not about the public revenue.
#ASSERT `Is the old offence abolished as regards what I did` `cheating` (Date 1 1 1969) FALSE
-- Cheating relating to the public revenue is kept.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the old offence abolished as regards what I did` `cheating` (Date 1 1 1969) TRUE)
-- Not one of the old offences.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the old offence abolished as regards what I did` `none of these` (Date 1 1 1980) FALSE)
-- A Schedule 3 Part I offence to the extent stated there.
#ASSERT `Is the old offence abolished as regards what I did` `an offence under an enactment mentioned in Part I of Schedule 3, to the extent it depends on a section or part of a section in column 3 of that Schedule` (Date 1 1 1969) FALSE

§§ `Section 35 -- commencement`

-- The Act came into force on 1 January 1969.
#ASSERT (`When did the Theft Act 1968 come into force`) EQUALS Date 1 1 1969
-- The Act was passed on 26 July 1968, the date under the long title.
#ASSERT (`When was the Theft Act 1968 passed`) EQUALS Date 26 7 1968
-- The last part was the day before commencement.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the Theft Act 1968 apply to what I did` (Date 31 12 1968))
-- The last part was on the day of commencement.
#ASSERT `Does the Theft Act 1968 apply to what I did` (Date 1 1 1969)
-- Committed before commencement: s 27 applies as to a corresponding offence (s 35(2)).
#ASSERT `Does section 27 apply to the offence I am accused of committing before the Act came into force` (Date 31 12 1968)
-- Committed on the day of commencement.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 27 apply to the offence I am accused of committing before the Act came into force` (Date 1 1 1969))

§§ `Section 36 -- extent`

-- England and Wales (by the long title).
#ASSERT (`Does the Theft Act 1968 extend to where I am` `England and Wales`) EQUALS `the Act extends there`
-- Scotland (s 36(3)).
#ASSERT (`Does the Theft Act 1968 extend to where I am` `Scotland`) EQUALS `the Act does not extend there, by section 36(3)`
-- Northern Ireland (s 36(3)).
#ASSERT (`Does the Theft Act 1968 extend to where I am` `Northern Ireland`) EQUALS `the Act does not extend there, by section 36(3)`
-- The Isle of Man: the text says nothing. Not covered.
#ASSERT (`Does the Theft Act 1968 extend to where I am` `the Isle of Man`) EQUALS `the text does not say whether the Act extends there`
-- The Channel Islands: the text says nothing. Not covered.
#ASSERT (`Does the Theft Act 1968 extend to where I am` `the Channel Islands`) EQUALS `the text does not say whether the Act extends there`
-- Elsewhere: the text says nothing. Not covered.
#ASSERT (`Does the Theft Act 1968 extend to where I am` `outside the British postal area`) EQUALS `the text does not say whether the Act extends there`
