§ `Schedule 1`


§§ `Schedule 1 paragraph 2 -- taking or destroying fish`

-- Took fish from private water.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` TRUE TRUE
-- In public water.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` TRUE FALSE)
-- Took or destroyed nothing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` FALSE TRUE)
-- A fine not exceeding level 5 on summary conviction, nothing else.
#ASSERT (`What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `an offence, liable to the penalty the section states` `pen summary level 5 only`
-- Not an offence.
#ASSERT (`What is the most that can follow if I am convicted of unlawfully taking or destroying fish` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `no offence under this section on these facts`
-- Convicted, the thing was with me for the purpose.
#ASSERT `May the court order forfeiture of what I had with me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Not convicted.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court order forfeiture of what I had with me` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- The thing was not with me for the purpose.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the court order forfeiture of what I had with me` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Committing, or reasonably suspected of committing, the offence.
#ASSERT `May any person arrest me without warrant` TRUE
-- Neither.
#ASSERT NOT (`May any person arrest me without warrant` FALSE)
-- Committing the offence and the thing liable to forfeiture.
#ASSERT `May any person seize what I had with me` TRUE TRUE
-- The thing would not be liable to forfeiture.
#ASSERT NOT (`May any person seize what I had with me` TRUE FALSE)
-- Not committing the offence.
#ASSERT NOT (`May any person seize what I had with me` FALSE TRUE)
